  "goodToKnow": "Der Genosse (die Genossin) is a comrade. Social Democrats in the SPD traditionally call each other Genossen, as did members of the GDR's ruling SED. The word originally meant someone sharing in something, related to genießen (to enjoy). It also appears in der Zeitgenosse (contemporary), der Eidgenosse (Swiss confederate) and die Genossenschaft (cooperative). Weak noun: den Genossen. Plural: die Genossen."
